{"id":"8ed33d21-3119-4b36-91e3-0ae0f78090b2","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8771311f326000e1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/live-run.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0059ec7ba126cf81a88dfba8f409a0078e3f413d","start":1577,"end":1602},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","SAME_TEXT_MS","=","1000"]},"context":{"before":"5afc2303f36503bb","after":"4c656718d45ecead"}},"payload":{"text":"A run of the same text started this recently (the interval's, or the save before) isn't started again by a save.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:50.042Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:50.042Z"}
{"id":"8f312e83-81b5-42bb-ba0f-17e009f1823c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"21361ca67fdb5fae","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/live-run.ts","baseline":{"blob":"61596764ac591be457896dc68a5df616fc153feb","start":0,"end":64},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","appRootOf","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/lifecycle","\""]},"context":{"after":"0b63740c2729e487"}},"payload":{"text":"Live runs (RUNTIME-EVIDENCE.md, *Live runs*): the file you're editing runs again on each save, and on an interval once it's\nbeen edited while its text differs from what its last run ran, so the Margin stays current. It's a debug session like any\nother, but quiet (no toolbar, status bar, view or console, stopping at nothing, not in the running list) and harmless:\nnobody is watching, so it asks nothing (the debug worker's `live`). An edit stops the one going. None starts while a run of\nyours of the same file is going, since that's what its Margin shows, and starting one of yours stops a live one. Off with\n`run.liveRuns`; the interval is `run.liveRuns.interval` (seconds, 0: saves only).\n\nVS Code binds F5 to starting only while nothing's debugging, and a live run counts: pressed just after a save, F5 would do\nnothing. So while only live runs are going, `run.liveGoing` binds it (this extension's package.json). And it opens the Debug\nConsole on a page's first session, which any session that never opens it would use up — a live run, a test file run from\nFeatures and tests, a terminal's `node` — and the run of yours after them would end unseen, the console opened later showing\nthe first of the ended ones: the first of yours is told to open it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:53.859Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:53.859Z"}
{"id":"90cae6d0-5532-4213-997c-008d0fd30265","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2b0c697957eb6f54","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/live-run.ts","baseline":{"blob":"af48670bff0cd3e641727ccd3c143940d6ad357b","start":8223,"end":8261},"shape":{"type":"MemberExpression","atoms":["vscode",".","workspace",".","onDidSaveTextDocument"]},"context":{"before":"24d0be82c090fc4a","after":"df57accd005343e8"}},"payload":{"text":"A save runs it: the last of a burst of saves, unless that text started a run just now.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:13.977Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:13.977Z"}
{"id":"94152e91-74cc-465b-9d10-0736167c27c3","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6be4fd2864c66433","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/live-run.ts","baseline":{"blob":"169a91dce2a56d623429cce04c64fccf06433dfa","start":3098,"end":3162},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","last","=","new","Map","<","string",",","{","\"","text","\"",":","string",";","\"","at","\"",":","number","}",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"0a23ba6c481ab1c3","after":"679576b7488d451e"}},"payload":{"text":"What each file's last live run ran, and when it started.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:38.313Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:38.313Z"}
